    description: "Tamarind pulihora is the standard prasadam and festival rice of Godavari households, cooked for Sankranti, Dasara and temple offerings and always carried on journeys. In Konaseema it is made with gingelly oil and a sharp, well-reduced tamarind paste so it keeps well for a day or two. Substitutions: sesame oil (gingelly) → untoasted sesame oil from Indian grocers (Do not use toasted East Asian sesame oil; it is too strong.); tamarind block → tamarind concentrate (Use about 2 tbsp concentrate diluted in 150 ml water.). Storage: Keeps at cool room temperature for a day and in the fridge for 3 days; the tamarind paste alone keeps 3 weeks refrigerated. Serve at room temperature rather than reheating.",
