    title: "Patodi Rassa", category: "main",
    description: "Patodi rassa is a celebratory dish of the Varhadi kitchen of Vidarbha, where gram-flour preparations take the place of meat at vegetarian feasts. Its fiery, oil-topped gravy built on roasted dry coconut, garlic and chilli is typical of the Nagpur and Amravati belt. Substitutions: Dry coconut (kopra) → Unsweetened desiccated coconut (Roast it gently; it browns faster than kopra.); Goda or kala masala → Garam masala plus 1/4 tsp ground cloves (Less smoky but close enough.); Poppy seeds → Cashews or sunflower seeds (Poppy seeds are restricted in some countries such as the UAE.). Storage: Store rassa and patodi separately in the fridge for up to 2 days; combine only when reheating so the patodi does not turn mushy.",
